From: (xbox360 netboot session)
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] net: sis190: fix lost TX queue wakeup on SMP (Xbox 360)

On the Xbox 360 (Xenon, 6 hardware threads) the TX ring fills during bulk NFS
writes and the queue is never woken again: the stop in sis190_start_xmit()
and the wake in sis190_tx_interrupt() race on different CPUs with only
smp_wmb/smp_rmb ordering, and the irq side only wakes when it saw the ring
full at entry. Result: NETDEV WATCHDOG, NFS root hangs, hung-task panic.

Use full barriers on both sides and wake whenever the queue is stopped and
there is room. Tested: Debian NFS root boots and runs Xfce; previously died
within 30 s of boot.

---
--- drivers/net/ethernet/sis/sis190.c.xenon-orig	2026-10-25 11:44:34.459761054 -0700
+++ drivers/net/ethernet/sis/sis190.c	2026-10-25 11:44:34.475637879 -0700
@@ -726,10 +726,17 @@
 
 	if (tp->dirty_tx != dirty_tx) {
 		tp->dirty_tx = dirty_tx;
-		smp_wmb();
-		if (queue_stopped)
+		/*
+		 * Pairs with the smp_mb() in sis190_start_xmit(): make the
+		 * new dirty_tx visible before we look at the queue state, so
+		 * a stop racing with this cleanup is always followed by a wake.
+		 */
+		smp_mb();
+		if (netif_queue_stopped(dev) &&
+		    (READ_ONCE(tp->cur_tx) - dirty_tx) < NUM_TX_DESC)
 			netif_wake_queue(dev);
 	}
+	(void)queue_stopped;
 }
 
 /*
@@ -1250,11 +1257,12 @@
 
 	SIS_W32(TxControl, 0x1a00 | CmdReset | CmdTxEnb);
 
-	dirty_tx = tp->dirty_tx;
+	dirty_tx = READ_ONCE(tp->dirty_tx);
 	if ((tp->cur_tx - NUM_TX_DESC) == dirty_tx) {
 		netif_stop_queue(dev);
-		smp_rmb();
-		if (dirty_tx != tp->dirty_tx)
+		/* Pairs with the smp_mb() in sis190_tx_interrupt(). */
+		smp_mb();
+		if ((tp->cur_tx - READ_ONCE(tp->dirty_tx)) < NUM_TX_DESC)
 			netif_wake_queue(dev);
 	}
 out:
